# Bug 06, witness A (the spoteffects() FIXME): polymon() keeps running
# after a nested rehumanize(), so retouch_equipment(2) runs twice for one
# polymorph.  This is the keystream recorded in session.json.
#
# A level-0 form gets only rnd(4) hit points (polyself.c:866) while lava
# does d(6,6), so the poly form always dies inside polymon()'s own
# spoteffects() call (polyself.c:972).  lava_effects() reaches losehp()
# only via `Wwalking && dmg < u.uhp` -- and that test reads the HUMAN hp
# while losehp() decrements u.mh, which is why a healthy hero in a frail
# form passes it and then loses the form.
#
# Fireproof boots are required: lava_effects() burns organic boots away
# BEFORE testing Wwalking, which would drop the hero into the lava.
# A wand (not a potion) of polymorph is required: destroyable() lets fire
# destroy potions/scrolls/spellbooks but not wands.
#
# The Eye of the Aethiopica makes the duplicate pass visible.  It is a
# quest artifact of the WRONG role (Wizard) but the RIGHT alignment
# (neutral), so badclass is true and badalign is false: touch_artifact()
# blasts unconditionally yet retouch_object() still returns 1, leaving
# the amulet worn for the second pass to blast again.
#
# Evidence in the recording: TWO d(2,10) @ touch_artifact(artifact.c:953)
# after one polymorph.  Control: seed4247 (same but no lava) has ONE.

seed: 4242
datetime: 20000110090000
nethackrc: |
  OPTIONS=name:r,role:Valkyrie,race:human,gender:female,align:neutral
  OPTIONS=playmode:debug
  OPTIONS=!autopickup
  OPTIONS=!tutorial
  OPTIONS=pettype:none
  OPTIONS=time,showexp

"\x1b#levelchange\n30\n                             "
"\x17fireproof water walking boots\n"
"\x17The Eye of the Aethiopica\n "
"\x17ring of polymorph control\n"
"\x17wand of polymorph\nWePf Pgr"
"\x17lava\nzh.kobold\n    "
